A||N||1||FieroJoe||Isuzu Backup Light switch adjustment?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||04-25-2001||10:15 PM||||Well, I now have a problem similar to what squoach had.  Both of my back up lights do not come on.  I have tried moving the shifter around, no use.  I took apart the connector and jumpered it and the backup lights came on, so I know that all the connections from C500 are good (I had previously taken it apart so that is why I was leary of it being bad).  I put my DVOM leads on the switch side of the connector, had my dad put it into reverse, and there was no connection made.<P>Now I understand that with earlier trannys (4spd muncies?) the switch is underneat the center console, and can be easily adjusted.  This switch resides on top of the tranny case.  I tried a few searches, but the only "backup light switch adjustment" topics were about turning the screw underneat the center console.<P>So, is there an adjustment for this one?  Or does it just need to be replaced?  If replacement is the way, what can I expect to pay for a new one?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-26-2001||11:56 AM||||There is no adjustment. The switch is bad and must be replaced. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
